{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013e2bAAcApK4JhQhxpHuX8h","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"7a172083f27035a8f20aa71fbc5e208ab07fa97a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T10:00:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"HEAD -> main\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f91a68e8c8dcdef4969050d70ac6d9c7e1bb5792\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T11:32:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Properly handle the manifest returned via pacote\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"5473276ce7e70c460e15b43a27f500dc452e6aa4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-06T17:21:26Z\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v11.0.0\",\"refs\":\"tag: v11.0.0\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"549c8a2165dce773cc63343bf48d7ebbd43d942f\",\"date\":\"2026-10-05T18:35:42-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Stop generating unused build manifests (#1935)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Remove StatsWriterPlugin from the Webpack and Rspack configurations so builds no longer emit *.buildmanifest.json. These manifests supported offline mode and are no longer consumed by core.\\n\\nRemove the unused webpack-stats-plugin dependency from both configuration packages and the openmrs CLI, and update the lockfile.\\nCoordinate rollout with patient-chart’s Angular form-entry app, whose custom Webpack configuration still imports this plugin through the tooling’s transitive dependency.\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"b439966ee59c5a9d0cc569942c6fb6d98bb28ba4\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T18:01:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Rewrite the openmrs CLI README around how it's used (#1905)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"240212209388de52b020bdad3d5760f23946e451\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T23:56:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt the shared Prettier configuration (#1892)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a2a536e17fb35333b26552436803d3a34df75ef2\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T21:44:28+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Check IPv4 loopback explicitly when selecting ports (#1915)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"537fb7b349faddd5785b4800a97f7bb9fa65b6ef\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T21:39:47+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Stop precompressing source maps in openmrs build (#1916)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"40f9d18356ecf03dabd43996f5f205ef7e59c2bd\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T12:11:09+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Let openmrs develop pick a port on hosts without IPv6 (#1903)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"isPortAvailable binds the port on both localhost and ::1, and treated any\\nerror from the ::1 bind as the port being taken. On a host with IPv6\\ndisabled, that bind fails with EAFNOSUPPORT for every port, so\\n`openmrs develop --port <n>` always reported the port as in use and\\n`openmrs develop` without --port scanned every port up to 65535 and gave\\nup.\\n\\nWe now only treat the ::1 bind as a conflict when the error means\\nsomething is actually listening there. EAFNOSUPPORT (IPv6 disabled) and\\nEADDRNOTAVAIL (IPv6 enabled but no ::1 on the loopback) fall back to the\\nIPv4 result.\\n\\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0119NcFRAE7ZNsubL4edUik3\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"a62f8164991a64135f438cef848fdc751e866d20\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:08:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework (#1894)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (BREAKING) Remove offline & rxjs support from framework\\n\\nRetains a small compatibility shim with the most commonly-used public\\nfunctions now stubbed. These deprecated shims will be removed in a\\nfuture version.\\n\\nThe biggest breaking change is the framework no longer supports rxjs\\ndirectly. Functions that returned Observables now return Promises. A\\nsmall compatibility patch is provided for the notifications system.\\n\\n* Fix `getCurrentUser`'s opts\\n\\n* Remove isLoginEnabled\\n\\n* Sounder re-implementation of getCurrentUser()\\n\\n* Remove more stuff, add back a couple of drop APIs we need, and re-add mocks\\n\\n* More clean-up\\n\\n* Add a changeset gentle-jars-pull.md\\n\\n* (chore) Add docs\\n\\n* Clean-up README and _main-content.scss\\n\\n* Fixup changesets\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3b9970b4c3f70749ecb5421e4d14de412c35ee70\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T14:37:29-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Mitigate malicious tarballs in assemble command\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb\",\"date\":\"2026-09-10T14:20:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\\n\\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\\nbasically ensuring we're using a consistent browserlist.\\n\\nThis also removes the \\\"main\\\" chunk we were generating, but which was\\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\\nloader and then the index chunk.\\n\\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\\n\\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\\n\\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\\n\\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\\n\\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\\n\\n* Create changeset\\n\\n* Fix failing test on CI\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"829be67a51e473609382150db0a33e3f99e450e3\",\"date\":\"2026-09-09T02:57:21-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) O3-5853: Use browserslist to compile JS in modern format (#1868)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2edf609e742b5517239da376db482747d5da5eb9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-03T16:21:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Fail assemble by default if things are obviously broken (#1795)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e6ec8408448ca34a63fe22b310c9c3cb0006b2f1\",\"date\":\"2026-08-29T00:13:11+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#1860)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9f0c6aa831f37ffcaf167a7096b07ec3e96a0431\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:13:19-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add a distribution-controlled version property (#1815)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"16a6c01d099267045f174f95ecf3936d3b770fb9\",\"date\":\"2026-08-07T13:46:52-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) O3-5872: Add support for static compression of frontend (#1838)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T23:19:08+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\\n\\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\\nthe natural first adopter.\\n\\nWhat changed:\\n\\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\\n  the shared config now provides.\\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\\n\\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\\nintroduced no new findings.\\n\\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\\n\\nWith flat config, 'eslint src' lints JavaScript files too, but the lint\\ntask only hashed src/**/*.{ts,tsx}. In practice turbo 2.5.2 still\\ninvalidated the cache on .js changes (its hashing treats the glob more\\npermissively than its dry-run input listing reports), but that safety\\nlooks accidental, so this makes the inputs match what actually gets\\nlinted. Also adds the .storybook and mocks directories that the\\nstorybook workspace lints, which were never covered by src/**.\\n\\n* Add a changeset for the ESLint 9 migration\\n\\nPatch-level for the packages whose published source changed. The changes\\nare comment-only removals of stale eslint-disable directives, so there is\\nno functional impact on consumers.\\n\\n* Regenerate the API docs\\n\\nRemoving the stale eslint-disable comment lines shifted source line\\nnumbers, and the generated docs embed 'Defined in' links with line\\nanchors. All 42 changed files are line-number link updates only.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"401e227eaf324ce8d2eb6332a411a6b8e5f86067\",\"date\":\"2026-06-09T10:17:39+05:30\",\"message\":\"(chore) Release v10.0.0 (#1794)\",\"refs\":\"tag: v10.0.0\",\"body\":\"* (chore): Release v10.0.0\\n\\n* (chore) Update @openmrs/esm-framework peerDependency to 10.x\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Bump internal @openmrs/esm-* peerDependencies to 10.x\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n* (chore) Use workspace:^ for internal @openmrs/esm-* peerDependencies\\n\\nLets the published peer range track the package version automatically\\n(rewritten to ^X.Y.Z by yarn npm publish) instead of hand-bumping N.x\\neach major release.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"authorName\":\"Nethmi Rodrigo\",\"authorEmail\":\"nethmi@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"fce9c4b688eb9b26df7f8354e1a30532640137cf\",\"date\":\"2026-05-23T00:12:23+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Sort package names with localeCompare\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Use an explicit localeCompare comparator when listing available package names in resolvePackages error messages. This satisfies SonarCloud's new-code reliability rule without changing package resolution behavior.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f5fff6640b1fe94ca5b18e65e50f23ba98b2363f\",\"date\":\"2026-04-18T07:10:42-04:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Add support to invoke develop with package name (#1750)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1dcccfd421c94ee0f0a8aa6c7c974cadab3d5fb8\",\"date\":\"2026-04-15T09:22:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(BREAKING) Drop IMO and don't load arbitrary content in production mode (#1743)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"}],\"totalCount\":22}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b24b2fa-9c82-4462-9f7e-1618466fdc7c","uuid":"fe014525-0448-43f3-a3c4-9a68f0aa2fcf","timestamp":"2026-10-23T18:16:19.443Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"commits\":[{\"hash\":\"7a172083f27035a8f20aa71fbc5e208ab07fa97a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-10T10:00:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using NPM trusted-publication\",\"refs\":\"HEAD -> main\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f91a68e8c8dcdef4969050d70ac6d9c7e1bb5792\",\"date\":\"2026-10-08T11:32:31-04:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Properly handle the manifest returned via pacote\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\